WEBVTT

00:10.040 --> 00:11.280
Come on in.

00:11.280 --> 00:13.490
Welcome to the library café, Moon Reader.

00:15.360 --> 00:16.120
Hello.

00:16.120 --> 00:18.160
Oh, Owner.

00:19.810 --> 00:21.080
Touya.

00:24.040 --> 00:26.040
So how's the café going?

00:26.040 --> 00:27.910
It's going very well.

00:27.910 --> 00:31.840
The girls seem full of life, too,
now that they've found jobs.

00:31.840 --> 00:33.440
Sorry for the wait.

00:31.840 --> 00:33.440
Thanks for your order.

00:34.930 --> 00:36.710
Same goes for us, too, of course.

00:36.710 --> 00:38.760
We're keeping it well guarded!

00:38.760 --> 00:40.730
Great, thanks.

00:41.240 --> 00:43.750
<i>The business idea came to me on a whim,</i>

00:43.750 --> 00:45.730
<i>but I guess it was the right choice.</i>

00:46.530 --> 00:49.460
<i>The trader, Olba-san, really helped out</i>

00:50.430 --> 00:54.780
<i>by paying a high price for the bicycles 
I mass-produced at the Workshop.</i>

00:57.620 --> 00:59.780
<i>Thanks to him, we got everything together.</i>

01:05.650 --> 01:09.750
The books that Linze bought for us 
have been especially popular with women.

01:09.750 --> 01:10.660
Wow.

01:10.660 --> 01:12.300
Everyone seems to be enjoying it.

01:12.300 --> 01:13.640
That's great.

01:13.640 --> 01:15.760
Buying books is expensive, after all.

01:15.760 --> 01:19.770
We might be charging an entry fee, 
 but I figured it would be nice

01:19.770 --> 01:23.340
if people could enjoy a meal 
while casually reading like this.

01:24.070 --> 01:27.140
You made all the furnishings 
here yourself, right?

01:27.450 --> 01:29.150
Huh? Yeah.

01:29.150 --> 01:30.860
Must be nice.

01:32.040 --> 01:35.860
My late grandpa was able to use Null Magic,

01:36.270 --> 01:39.590
but I don't have any 
aptitudes, so I'm jealous.

01:39.590 --> 01:42.700
What kind of Null Magic 
did your grandpa have?

01:42.700 --> 01:46.660
He had the spell "Gravity," which let him 
make anything he touched heavier.

01:47.560 --> 01:48.870
Gravity?

01:49.170 --> 01:51.800
Well, it only made things a tiny bit heavier,

01:51.800 --> 01:54.630
so honestly, there wasn't 
much use for that spell.

01:55.410 --> 01:57.080
I don't think that's right.

01:57.080 --> 01:58.010
Huh?

01:58.010 --> 02:03.190
Depending on how it's used, 
that might be an ultimate-level spell.

03:34.980 --> 03:39.990
Episode 3

03:34.980 --> 03:39.990
Collecting Books and a Library Café

03:41.250 --> 03:43.160
An extermination date...

03:43.950 --> 03:45.650
I'm looking forward to it!

03:45.650 --> 03:48.290
That's an awfully violent date, though.

03:48.290 --> 03:49.710
It's fine!

03:49.710 --> 03:52.550
I'm happy to have you to myself,

03:52.550 --> 03:53.910
and besides...

03:53.910 --> 03:57.500
I want my Guild Card to 
be Red like everyone else's.

03:57.500 --> 03:58.750
I see.

04:01.030 --> 04:02.980
Bloody Crab?

04:02.980 --> 04:03.970
A crab?

04:04.560 --> 04:07.260
It's a red crab monster 
that has four large pincers

04:07.260 --> 04:11.180
and is known for its very hard shell.

04:11.580 --> 04:13.990
Its shell can be sold to make equipment from,

04:13.990 --> 04:16.650
and I hear its meat sells for a high price, too.

04:17.000 --> 04:20.590
Huh... I guess we'll accept 
this one for now, then.

04:31.290 --> 04:32.960
Um...

04:32.960 --> 04:37.290
Mr. Mochizuki, you're the owner of 
the library café, Moon Reader, right?

04:37.290 --> 04:39.710
Yeah, I am.

04:39.710 --> 04:41.920
My name is Prim.

04:41.920 --> 04:43.290
Prim-san.

04:43.290 --> 04:44.380
So, um,

04:44.380 --> 04:48.650
there's this series of books in the Refreese 
Imperium called <i>The Order of the Rose</i>.

04:48.650 --> 04:50.650
I was wondering if you had 
any plans to stock them?

04:50.650 --> 04:53.830
Uh, is that series already complete?

04:53.830 --> 04:56.810
Yes! It should be complete 
with 15 volumes in total!

04:57.260 --> 05:00.020
If it's complete, then... sure.

05:00.020 --> 05:01.690
I'll go ahead and order it.

05:01.690 --> 05:03.670
Thank you so much!

05:03.670 --> 05:05.940
I'm really, really looking forward to it!

05:09.370 --> 05:12.490
Prim-san was super happy about that.

05:13.130 --> 05:14.840
I guess she loves books?

05:16.000 --> 05:20.420
Touya, do you know what 
<i>The Order of the Rose</i> is about?

05:20.420 --> 05:23.260
No, I don't. Do you?

05:23.260 --> 05:24.940
Well, yes.

05:24.940 --> 05:27.320
It's a story about a nation's order of knights,

05:27.320 --> 05:29.400
depicting the conflict between 
the male-only Order of the Rose

05:29.400 --> 05:32.260
and the female-only Defenders of the Lily,

05:32.610 --> 05:34.930
as well as the romance that develops

05:34.930 --> 05:38.270
between the knights within 
the Order amidst that conflict.

05:40.710 --> 05:43.140
Within the Order? Huh?

05:43.140 --> 05:46.060
But all the knights are guys?

05:46.890 --> 05:47.740
Huh?

05:50.580 --> 05:51.530
Wait...

05:51.530 --> 05:57.080
Does that mean it's the same kind of book 
that Linze insisted on buying a lot of?

05:57.830 --> 05:59.410
I see...

05:59.410 --> 06:03.030
I did promise her, though, 
so it'd be wrong not to buy them.

06:03.030 --> 06:04.460
That's true.

06:06.220 --> 06:09.640
Still, I'm surprised you knew what 
kind of series <i>The Order of the Rose</i> was.

06:10.190 --> 06:12.960
Oh, well, you see...

06:12.960 --> 06:16.130
I actually know the author of those books.

06:16.130 --> 06:19.100
That's why I knew about the series.

06:19.100 --> 06:21.220
Huh? Who is it?

06:21.220 --> 06:23.080
Is it someone I know?

06:23.080 --> 06:26.070
No, I don't think you know her, Touya.

06:26.440 --> 06:30.520
She's famous, so she can't exactly 
publish under her real name,

06:30.520 --> 06:34.030
and she writes under the 
pen name of Riel Rifrese, but...

06:34.520 --> 06:36.370
you can't tell anyone else, okay?

06:37.180 --> 06:39.800
It's Reliel Rehn Refreese.

06:40.630 --> 06:43.210
The first princess of the Refreese Imperium.

06:44.410 --> 06:45.220
Huh?

06:45.700 --> 06:48.500
The Refreese Imperium 
and the Kingdom of Belfast

06:48.500 --> 06:52.980
have always been closely 
affiliated as fellow monarchies.

06:52.980 --> 06:56.060
So I've known Sister Riri for a long time now.

06:56.060 --> 06:59.290
I guess, at some point, 
she found herself into such things,

06:59.290 --> 07:02.090
and ultimately she began writing them herself.

07:02.090 --> 07:04.340
Ugh, I'm getting a headache.

07:06.940 --> 07:10.740
Well, let's go exterminate 
that Bloody Crab first.

07:11.850 --> 07:12.900
Hup!

07:12.900 --> 07:15.470
Go, go, go, go!

07:22.200 --> 07:24.160
So that's a Bloody Crab?

07:24.680 --> 07:26.110
It's huge.

07:26.640 --> 07:28.630
It looks as big as a dump truck.

07:28.630 --> 07:32.840
Entwine thus, Earth! 
Earthen Curse, Earthbind!

07:38.790 --> 07:39.520
Accel!

07:43.980 --> 07:45.060
Gravity!

07:52.470 --> 07:53.490
There.

07:53.810 --> 07:55.580
What did you do?

07:55.580 --> 07:58.890
I used a spell to double the crab's own weight.

07:58.890 --> 08:01.460
Its body became too heavy for it to move.

08:02.030 --> 08:05.420
This spell allows you to alter 
the weight of things you touch.

08:05.770 --> 08:08.760
Lack of magical capacity is 
probably why Will's grandpa

08:08.760 --> 08:11.350
could only make things slightly heavier.

08:11.740 --> 08:14.570
But with your vast magical capacity...

08:23.350 --> 08:25.530
Congratulations.

08:25.530 --> 08:29.660
With these points, Yumina's 
guild rank has gone up.

08:31.140 --> 08:33.660
Now I'm the same rank as everyone else.

08:33.660 --> 08:36.070
Yeah. That just leaves...

08:36.070 --> 08:37.190
Prim-san.

08:37.190 --> 08:38.530
Yes? What is it?

08:38.530 --> 08:41.410
I'm thinking of heading out 
to buy those books now.

08:41.410 --> 08:42.190
Huh?!

08:42.190 --> 08:44.560
So... if you wouldn't mind,

08:44.560 --> 08:46.940
I was wondering if you could 
list up some books from that genre

08:46.940 --> 08:48.710
that seem like they'd be popular.

08:48.710 --> 08:51.900
D-Does that mean you would 
buy and stock those books?!

08:51.900 --> 08:54.850
Yes, assuming they have the inventory.

08:54.850 --> 08:58.120
I'm good on money after the reward 
from that extermination quest.

08:58.120 --> 09:00.270
H-Hold on a moment, please!

09:01.270 --> 09:02.190
Everyone!

09:02.190 --> 09:05.610
Mr. Mochizuki said he'd 
stock up on the books we want!

09:05.610 --> 09:07.580
Huh?! No way?!

09:07.580 --> 09:09.050
Hold on, hold on!

09:09.050 --> 09:10.200
Really?!

09:10.200 --> 09:11.790
I can finally get that book I wanted?!

09:13.750 --> 09:15.600
Y-You're really okay with this?

09:15.600 --> 09:16.570
Oh, yeah.

09:16.570 --> 09:18.800
Th-Then they're all written down here.

09:19.390 --> 09:21.100
<i>The Order of the Rose</i>, all 15 volumes.

09:21.100 --> 09:23.020
<i>Butler's Secret</i>, all 5 volumes.

09:23.020 --> 09:25.550
<i>The Fallen Prince's Oath 
of Servitude</i>, all 8 volumes.

09:25.550 --> 09:27.450
<i>Boy in a Cage</i>, all 6 volumes.

09:27.450 --> 09:29.560
<i>A Sweet and Dangerous 
Embrace</i>, all 12 volumes.

09:29.560 --> 09:32.250
<i>Burning Nocturne: The Two Who 
Never Returned</i>, all 5 volumes.

09:32.250 --> 09:34.780
<i>The Mage and the Sweet Trap</i>, all 12 volumes.

09:34.780 --> 09:37.090
<i>The Immoral Bridegroom</i>, all 17 volumes.

09:37.090 --> 09:39.130
<i>Rose Magical</i>, all 9 volumes.

09:39.130 --> 09:42.060
And<i> Master Is Watching</i>, all 18 volumes!

09:43.410 --> 09:45.520
If you could please acquire them!

09:46.190 --> 09:50.480
Uh... I'll give it optimistic consideration.

09:51.520 --> 09:53.480
Yes!

09:53.480 --> 09:55.530
This is like a dream!

09:54.490 --> 09:57.980
Yumina, I want to go to Bern, 
the capital of Refreese,

09:57.980 --> 10:00.130
so would you share the memory with me?

10:00.130 --> 10:01.490
Of course.

10:27.180 --> 10:30.360
Excuse me. I'm looking for some books.

10:31.890 --> 10:33.650
Uh...

10:34.750 --> 10:36.430
The ones on this list.

10:36.430 --> 10:38.610
Sure. Let me take a look.

10:42.670 --> 10:47.790
Uh, you see, I'm looking for those books 
because my customers requested them.

10:47.790 --> 10:50.750
Oh, yes, I understand!

10:50.750 --> 10:54.470
We have the full collection of these, 
so please wait a little while!

10:56.160 --> 10:59.050
She definitely didn't understand me.

11:02.620 --> 11:04.760
This is an adventure tale.

11:04.760 --> 11:06.850
This one's a war chronicle?

11:08.810 --> 11:12.770
I need to stock up without 
leaning too heavily on one genre.

11:15.180 --> 11:18.770
At this rate, those sorts of books 
will take over the whole café.

11:18.820 --> 11:21.700
Y-You're sold out?!

11:21.700 --> 11:23.780
My apologies.

11:23.780 --> 11:26.470
This was the last of our inventory,

11:26.470 --> 11:28.910
and it's uncertain when 
we'll get our next shipment.

11:28.910 --> 11:32.080
No way!

11:32.080 --> 11:36.310
Oh, sir, I've retrieved 
all the books you ordered.

11:36.310 --> 11:37.970
Would you like these, as well?

11:37.970 --> 11:40.390
Oh, yes. I'd like them all, please.

11:41.050 --> 11:44.370
Huh? He's the one who bought <i>RoseMagi</i>?

11:47.310 --> 11:48.880
What seems to be the matter?

11:48.880 --> 11:49.990
Well...

11:50.630 --> 11:54.650
The final volume of <i>Rose Magical</i>, 
one of the series that you ordered,

11:55.060 --> 11:57.680
happened to be our last copy in stock.

11:58.150 --> 12:01.580
That customer there also 
came here to purchase it.

12:01.580 --> 12:03.080
Oh...

12:03.570 --> 12:04.660
Um...

12:04.660 --> 12:05.850
Excuse me!

12:05.850 --> 12:09.370
Would you be willing to let me have 
the final volume of <i>Rose Magical</i>?!

12:09.370 --> 12:12.260
Uh, but I came here to buy this, too.

12:12.260 --> 12:13.780
This is the last shop!

12:13.780 --> 12:16.270
All the other bookstores I tried are sold out!

12:17.480 --> 12:19.760
I'm sorry to hear that, but...

12:21.700 --> 12:23.760
You bought <i>The Order of the Rose</i>, too?

12:23.760 --> 12:26.780
Huh? Oh, well, yeah.

12:32.010 --> 12:33.070
Um...

12:33.810 --> 12:36.860
You have a good eye for titles, don't you?

12:36.860 --> 12:39.600
No. You have the wrong idea.

12:39.600 --> 12:42.130
I was asked to buy these. 
I'm not into them myself.

12:42.130 --> 12:44.450
Yes, I understand. I understand!

12:45.160 --> 12:48.410
<i>She definitely does not understand.</i>

12:48.410 --> 12:51.660
I see. Uh-huh.

12:57.010 --> 12:58.150
What is it?

13:00.430 --> 13:01.680
I have a deal for you.

13:01.680 --> 13:04.570
If you'll let me have the 
final volume of <i>RoseMagi</i>,

13:04.570 --> 13:07.660
I'll autograph every volume of 
<i>The Order of the Rose</i> for you.

13:07.660 --> 13:08.800
How about it?

13:08.800 --> 13:10.100
Huh?

13:10.100 --> 13:13.560
How would having you autograph 
them benefit me in any way?

13:13.910 --> 13:19.520
It would, because I'm the author of 
<i>The Order of the Rose</i>, Riel Rifrese!

13:20.280 --> 13:21.600
Oh?

13:22.620 --> 13:23.820
How nice.

13:23.820 --> 13:25.900
Hey! You don't believe me, do you?

13:32.300 --> 13:34.220
<i>I guess I can try sounding her out.</i>

13:35.580 --> 13:39.040
I suppose that would mean 
you're Princess Reliel, then.

13:39.040 --> 13:40.040
Huh?

13:42.470 --> 13:44.250
<i>I knew she was tricking me.</i>

13:45.970 --> 13:50.020
H... H-H-H-H-H-How do you know that?!

13:50.790 --> 13:51.760
Huh?

13:51.760 --> 13:55.290
E-Even my father doesn't know about that!

13:55.290 --> 13:57.010
Huh? Seriously?

13:57.010 --> 13:58.650
You're really her?

13:58.650 --> 14:01.480
Wh-What are you planning to do 
now that you've found me out?!

14:02.480 --> 14:04.300
You're going to blackmail me, 
use me as a stepping stone

14:04.300 --> 14:06.730
to get closer to my younger 
brother, the next emperor,

14:06.730 --> 14:09.750
and then steal his chastity 
and make this nation yours!

14:09.750 --> 14:10.830
Are you an idiot?!

14:11.160 --> 14:13.450
Ow! Wh-What was that for?!

14:13.450 --> 14:14.370
Shut up!

14:14.370 --> 14:17.750
If I hadn't heard about that from Yumina, 
I would have completely ignored you!

14:18.360 --> 14:22.960
Is this nation going to be okay with 
someone like you as the first princess?

14:22.960 --> 14:24.480
Yumina?

14:24.480 --> 14:26.420
You mean the Yumina from Belfast?

14:26.880 --> 14:28.790
Just who are you?

14:31.290 --> 14:33.330
I'm Mochizuki Touya.

14:33.330 --> 14:36.530
I'm the fiancée of Princess 
Yumina, Princess of Belfast.

14:36.530 --> 14:38.230
Though the engagement is still unofficial.

14:38.230 --> 14:40.840
What?! F-Fiancée?!

14:40.840 --> 14:43.680
Fiancée, as in... that girl is getting married?!

14:43.680 --> 14:46.640
Huh? But Yumina is a woman...

14:46.640 --> 14:47.520
Huh?

14:47.520 --> 14:49.450
Wait, is it a sham marriage?

14:49.450 --> 14:52.120
Are you really after the king himself?!

14:52.120 --> 14:53.330
No, I'm not!

14:53.330 --> 14:55.190
Ow!

14:55.190 --> 14:58.480
I'm just going to have to 
ask Yumina to explain.

15:00.450 --> 15:01.490
Yumina!

15:01.490 --> 15:03.880
It's been a while, Sister Riri.

15:05.090 --> 15:08.090
Here, the final volume of <i>Rose Magical</i>.

15:12.660 --> 15:14.300
Touya, did you...

15:14.300 --> 15:16.770
I went to the Workshop and copied it.

15:16.770 --> 15:19.330
Okay, that solves everything.

15:19.330 --> 15:22.480
I did pay the bookstore enough 
money for an extra copy, too.

15:22.480 --> 15:23.550
Are you sure?

15:23.550 --> 15:25.230
I thought you wanted it.

15:25.230 --> 15:27.790
I told you, you've got it all wrong!

15:27.790 --> 15:31.220
I came to buy these so I could 
stock them in my shop!

15:31.220 --> 15:33.070
I'm not interested in it myself!

15:34.200 --> 15:36.570
That's kind of a waste in its own wa—

15:40.740 --> 15:43.380
Never mind! It's nothing!

15:55.540 --> 15:59.680
Th-The epitome of bliss!

16:17.860 --> 16:20.410
Thank you so much, Mr. Mochizuki!

16:20.410 --> 16:23.530
This will be my reward for a hard day's work!

16:23.530 --> 16:25.090
It was nothing.

16:26.410 --> 16:28.850
This is quite the lineup!

16:28.850 --> 16:30.840
As expected of you, Touya!

16:30.840 --> 16:33.460
Expected of me? Really?

16:35.230 --> 16:38.260
Um, where is <i>Burning Nocturne: 
The Two Who Never Returned</i>?

16:38.260 --> 16:40.790
U-Uh...

16:41.730 --> 16:43.970
That series is over here.

16:43.970 --> 16:47.190
Though the latest release, volume 5, is 
on the recommendation shelf over there.

16:47.730 --> 16:49.950
She knows it by heart.

16:49.950 --> 16:53.060
Maybe I should just let Linze be the owner...

16:53.660 --> 16:55.270
Sorry.

16:55.270 --> 16:58.790
I still haven't memorized 
where the books are.

16:58.790 --> 17:00.040
It's fine.

17:00.040 --> 17:01.790
Your job is to guard the place, anyway.

17:02.200 --> 17:05.750
Oh, yeah. I wanted to thank you 
for teaching me that Gravity spell.

17:05.750 --> 17:06.710
Huh?

17:07.210 --> 17:11.600
Is there anything you want, 
or anything you want to do?

17:14.320 --> 17:15.970
Well, I...

17:17.470 --> 17:19.930
I want to get stronger!

17:19.930 --> 17:21.970
There's someone I want to protect.

17:21.970 --> 17:24.740
I want to become even 
stronger so I can do that.

17:24.740 --> 17:26.220
Not just with pure might!

17:26.220 --> 17:28.870
I want to become a man who can 
protect her from all kinds of things!

17:40.770 --> 17:42.360
Oh, now I get it.

17:42.360 --> 17:44.360
Someone you want to protect, huh?

17:48.210 --> 17:52.170
That's the story. So really put 
Will through the wringer, please.

17:52.170 --> 17:56.170
Yes, we knights will take full 
responsibility for training him up.

17:56.170 --> 17:58.130
Get as strong as you'd like.

17:58.130 --> 18:00.100
Y-Yes, sir!

18:00.100 --> 18:01.750
Let's begin right away.

18:06.810 --> 18:08.270
Oh, Touya?

18:08.270 --> 18:10.980
What's up? Did you need something here?

18:10.980 --> 18:12.260
Yeah.

18:12.260 --> 18:15.190
Will said he wanted to get stronger, 
so I brought him here.

18:15.190 --> 18:18.320
I'm done introducing him, 
so I was about to head home.

18:21.040 --> 18:23.310
Hey, so, Touya...

18:23.660 --> 18:27.430
If you're about to go home with Gate, 
do you want to go to Silver Moon?

18:27.430 --> 18:30.380
I worked up a sweat, so I'd like
 to take a dip in the hot spring.

18:30.690 --> 18:31.990
Sure. Let's go.

18:31.990 --> 18:33.380
Yay!

18:35.980 --> 18:38.380
This is so refreshing.

18:38.740 --> 18:39.720
How's it going?

18:39.720 --> 18:42.070
Have you been having any issues at all?

18:42.070 --> 18:43.600
The hot spring's not acting up?

18:43.990 --> 18:47.750
No problems. We're getting 
a good flow of customers, too.

18:47.750 --> 18:51.930
To be honest, we're earning more 
profit off the bath fees than the inn.

18:51.930 --> 18:54.900
At this rate, we're likely to become 
the bathhouse Silver Moon.

18:54.900 --> 18:57.300
Oh, long time no see.

18:57.300 --> 19:00.240
Hey, Zanac-san. You're here, too?

19:00.240 --> 19:03.170
Well, ever since this was built,

19:03.170 --> 19:05.850
everything feels off if 
I don't bathe morning and night.

19:05.850 --> 19:07.700
I'm a regular here now.

19:07.700 --> 19:10.970
Zanac here even started 
recommending our hot spring

19:10.970 --> 19:14.420
to the customers visiting 
Fashion King Zanac.

19:14.420 --> 19:16.430
That's good to hear.

19:17.520 --> 19:20.500
Maybe I could collect an agent's fee?

19:22.050 --> 19:26.610
Oh, right. I finished another one of 
the outfit designs I received from you!

19:26.610 --> 19:27.350
Huh?

19:27.350 --> 19:30.970
I think it turned out quite well myself.

19:30.970 --> 19:33.980
I happened to bring the 
prototype with me today.

19:33.980 --> 19:34.940
Want to see it?

19:36.920 --> 19:39.780
Well, rather than just see it...

19:45.220 --> 19:46.660
So, what's this?

19:57.880 --> 20:00.380
That's right! It's a present from me!

20:00.920 --> 20:04.840
Yeah, you look good in it. Really cute.

20:06.300 --> 20:08.640
Wh-What are you saying?!

20:08.640 --> 20:12.230
You even changed out my 
clothes without asking! Jeez!

20:13.030 --> 20:16.030
<i>Even though she actually 
loves to wear cute clothes,</i>

20:16.030 --> 20:19.190
<i>she's probably convinced herself 
she doesn't look good in them.</i>

20:19.700 --> 20:25.240
<i>That's exactly why I thought I had to 
almost force her to wear it like this.</i>

20:26.410 --> 20:29.370
Well? Will you accept it?

20:31.830 --> 20:32.870
Look out!

20:43.090 --> 20:44.760
Is it hard to walk?

20:44.760 --> 20:47.050
Should we swap out just the shoes?

20:47.870 --> 20:50.620
It's fine like this.

20:51.170 --> 20:55.180
Touya, thank you for this present.

20:58.370 --> 20:59.860
<i>A lot may have happened,</i>

21:00.330 --> 21:02.490
<i>but all's well that ends well.</i>

21:03.180 --> 21:05.120
<i>This was a great day.</i>

21:12.280 --> 21:14.530
So peaceful.

21:14.530 --> 21:15.620
Sure is.

21:16.440 --> 21:18.580
U-Um, Touya!

21:18.960 --> 21:20.650
What is it, Linze?

21:22.250 --> 21:26.210
This is Riel Rifrese's new series.

21:26.210 --> 21:26.880
Huh?

21:26.880 --> 21:29.800
The first volume went on sale the other day,

21:29.800 --> 21:32.100
and volume two is scheduled 
to be out next month.

21:32.100 --> 21:33.870
Wow.

21:36.060 --> 21:38.490
The story is, well...

21:38.490 --> 21:40.770
It's about a man with almighty power

21:41.110 --> 21:43.100
who's out to take over a nation,

21:43.100 --> 21:45.940
so he gets that nation's knight, 
their beautiful princess,

21:45.940 --> 21:49.770
and her younger brother, the prince, 
in his clutches one by one,

21:49.770 --> 21:52.250
rising up the ladder.

21:52.250 --> 21:54.280
She claims, "I had sudden inspiration!"

21:54.280 --> 21:57.670
And rumors say she's 
writing it at a crazy pace...

21:57.670 --> 22:00.630
Yes, yes, yes!

22:01.480 --> 22:04.130
Sister Riri, did you...

22:05.360 --> 22:08.550
Next time I see that rotten head of hers,

22:09.310 --> 22:14.170
I'll have to give it a Gravity-enhanced chop!
